## Implemented behavior

`AcquireExperimentExclusionAsync` continues to acquire the same global Track0 measurement gate first. If the concrete manager has an `IControlledBenchmarkGuardian`, it then calls `SuspendAsync` before returning admission to experiment work. Its async lease calls `ResumeAsync` with `CancellationToken.None` and only reopens the global gate in `finally`, so caller cancellation cannot skip reconciliation or allow a competing benchmark before reconciliation completes.

The regression uses the real `GuardianSessionHost` contract with a deterministic runner. It proves a running specialized Guardian is stopped/reset on generic experiment admission, a desired instance change made during the experiment remains deferred, and release starts the latest desired instance. It also snapshots Track0 generation before/while/after the experiment and proves generation remains unchanged and Idle: generic experiment exclusion does not falsely report a controlled benchmark.

## Boundaries and exact continuation

This is primitive-level support. `GenericGuardianWindowsSessionCanaryExecutor` still uses a default unconnected `ControlledBenchmarkLeaseManager` when a runtime does not inject one. There is no complete generic runtime owner yet, so it is not valid to claim every product canary already suspends the specialized Guardian.

Next, build the concrete generic runtime owner that composes workload observation, supported classifier/eligibility, session budget/catalog, admitted executor and lifecycle KEEP ownership while injecting the same Guardian-connected benchmark manager used by the application. Prove fixed lock ordering and no deadlock across Track0 gate, specialized Guardian suspend/reconcile, DG exclusive admission, admitted Track2 mutation and lifecycle teardown. Retained leases must restore before rebind/retirement.

Activation remains blocked independently by missing production scene/mode/load/environment evidence: FF/FF MAX `CanaryContextEvidence=false`. External registry/vendor/driver mutation sources remain outside current authority. Windows/real-game HIL is required before any activation. Track6 item3 remains IN PROGRESS; item4 reliability and item5 post-session queue remain pending.

This documentary commit itself requires a fresh exact-head Windows CI before being marked GREEN.
